			"id": "agent-analysis-backup-extension-ability-entry",
			"interpretation": "EntryBackupAbility.ets is the module's declared backup/restore seam: it extends @kit.CoreFileKit BackupExtensionAbility with log-only onBackup/onRestore stubs; onRestore branches on bundleVersion.name starting '0.0.0.0' (comment-marked HarmonyOS-to-NEXT migration) versus other scenarios. It is reachable only via declarative wiring: module.json5 registers it as type 'backup' with srcEntry pointing at this file, exported:false, and metadata ohos.extension.backup referencing $profile:backup_config, whose allowToBackupRestore:true opts the module into backup restore. The UI side is independent: EntryAbility (mainElement) loads 'pages/Index' per main_pages.json; Index is a RelativeContainer whose @State message toggles 'Hello World' to 'Welcome' on click. Maintenance contract: keep srcEntry strings, $profile resource names, and exported class names synchronized; honor onRestore's documented synchronous-await contract for async work; keep the placeholder hypium suites under src/test and src/ohosTest resolvable; oh-package dependencies are empty, so @kit.* imports must resolve from the SDK; release obfuscation stays disabled though obfuscation-rules.txt holds -enable rules.",
			"kind": "analysis",
			"limitations": ["Whether the OS backup framework ever invokes onBackup/onRestore for this module, and whether allowToBackupRestore:true actually enables system backup, is unproved: the SDK framework contract was not executed or observed, only the declared registration was read.","Buildability is unproved: hvigor and the @ohos/hvigor-ohos-plugin hapTasks pipeline were never run, so the claim that hapTasks plus the @kit.* imports compile into a HAP for targets 'default' and 'ohosTest' remains an inference from configuration text.","The meaning of the '0.0.0.0' bundleVersion.name prefix as a HarmonyOS-to-NEXT migration marker is asserted only by in-file comments; it was not verified against CoreFileKit BundleVersion documentation.","The effect of the empty mock-config.json5 object and of the -enable-* rules in obfuscation-rules.txt while release obfuscation has enable:false is inferred, not demonstrated."],
